,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Verify GET /rest/api/3/project/search against live Jira Cloud REST docs — confirm it exists, the pagination model (startAt vs nextPageToken vs cursor), and the envelope keys (values[].key, isLast) — and cite the doc/observed response; if unverifiable, route the endpoint choice through a short spike before committing the preflight.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach quotes: 'GET /rest/api/3/project/search (paginated via startAt with the response envelope's values[].key / isLast)'","search_files '/rest/api/3/project' returns no matches in src/rebar — this is a NEW endpoint surface, not a reuse of an already-driven path","acli_graph.py:265 documents 'POST /rest/api/3/search endpoint is RETIRED (HTTP 410). The replacement /rest/api/3/search/jql paginates via an opaque nextPageToken' — direct in-repo evidence that (a) Cloud endpoints get deprecated and (b) pagination models differ from the classic startAt asserted here","Evidence class: endpoint SURFACE = Unverified (transport itself is Verified: _direct_rest_get at acli_rest.py:207 is real and used by get_issue_property/transition_issue/validate_assignee_exists)"],"finding":"The plan depends on the external Jira Cloud endpoint GET /rest/api/3/project/search and its pagination/envelope contract (startAt paging, values[].key, isLast) but this endpoint surface is UNVERIFIED against live Jira docs and is not used anywhere in the current codebase, while the repo already carries evidence that a sibling Cloud search endpoint was retired (POST /rest/api/3/search → HTTP 410) and its replacement paginates via an opaque nextPageToken rather than startAt — so the asserted pagination model itself may be wrong for project/search.","gr